  "strategy": "### 1. Approach and rationale\nWe propose a two-phase optimization strategy combining convex relaxation with local search. The approach addresses the nonconvexity of the overlap objective by:\n\n1. Relaxing the problem into a convex form for initial exploration\n2. Using a secondary local search to refine the solution\n3. Leveraging the initial_h_values as a structured starting point\n4. Maintaining feasibility through exact projection steps\n\nThe strategy balances global exploration via the convex solver with detailed local optimization. By detecting multiple correlation peaks and addressing them sequentially, the method systematically reduces the maximum overlap.\n\n### 2. Mathematical specification\n**Variables**:\n- h(x) \u2208 [0,1], \u222b\u2080\u00b2 h(x) dx = 1\n- Discretization: h \u2208 \u211d\u207f, sum(h) = n/2\n\n**Objective**:\nC\u2085 = max_k [conv(h, 1-h, mode='full')[k] * dx]\n\n**Constraints**:\n1. h[i] \u2208 [0, 1] for all i\n2. \u2211h[i] = n/2\n\n**Surrogate Problem**:\nDefine a sequence of convex subproblems where we fix all peaks in the correlation spectrum except one. Solve for h that minimizes each peak while maintaining feasibility.\n\n### 3. Implementation procedure\n**1. Initialization**:\na. Use initial_h_values if available, ensuring validity\nb. Else, construct symmetric h with n/2 points\nc. Compute initial C\u2085 and validate feasibility\n\n**2. Phase 1 - Convex Relaxation**:\nFor k in lag ranges:\n   i. Construct a convex approximation of the objective focusing on lag k\n   ii. Use CVXPY to solve the relaxed problem\n   iii. Track intermediate solutions\n\n**3. Phase 2 - Local Refinement**:\na. For each candidate from Phase 1:\n   i. Apply a gradient-based local search\n   ii. Compute exact C\u2085\n   iii. Update best solution\n\n**4. Projection and Feasibility**:\na. After each update, project h onto [0,1]\nb. Adjust magnitude to maintain sum(h) = n/2\n\n**5. Termination and Validation**:\na. Monitor time budget\nb. Ensure final solution meets constraints\nc. Compute final C\u2085 using exact metric\n\n### 4. Search choices and useful variations\n- Subproblem selection: Highest overlap peaks first\n- Gradient descent steps: Adaptive learning rate\n- Feasibility restoration: Exact projection onto [0,1] simplex\n\n### 5. Compute budget and robustness\n- Phase 1: O(np.log n)\n- Phase 2: O(mn) with m << n\n- Feasibility checks and projections O(n)\n\n### 6. Validation and return contract\n- Ensure sum(h) = n/2 to 1e-9 precision\n- Verify all h[i] \u2208 [0,1]\n- Recompute C\u2085 using exact cross-correlations",
